  "caption": "Figure 3: Top: Illustration of two-phase training for few-shot learning in Faster R-CNN. In phase 1, all blocks are trained. In phase 2, part of the model is frozen while others are fine-tuned. TFA Wang et al. (2020) and DeFRCN Qiao et al. (2021) follow this pipeline. For TFA, only the top-layer of the bounding box classifier and regressor are fine-tuned. For DeFRCN, the whole model is fine-tuned except for the convolutions in the bounding box classifier and regressor. Bottom: Left is the original structure for the RPN in Faster R-CNN; right is our CoRPN’s, consisting of cooperating bounding box classifiers. Note that we only add multiple classifier heads that share features, so the model complexity of CoRPN’s does not significantly exceeds a regular RPN. For convenience, we use the term RPN and RPN classifier interchangeably.",
